    "bodyHtml": "<h2>What it is</h2>\n<p>A Bio-ferment (Biole) is a fermented liquid organic fertilizer: liquid organic materials worked\non by Mountain Microorganisms — yeast, fungi and bacteria — which transform them into plant\nelements, vitamins, organic acids and other growth substances. Sprayed on the crop, the\nnutrients are absorbed through the leaves right away. It is a microbial soup that re-establishes\nthe ecosystem&#39;s microbial balance and makes plants more resistant to pests and disease.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>On the Nutritive Cycle:</strong> Biole is an <em>all-stages</em> input — a balanced backbone tonic that\nnourishes crops and steadies soil microbial life throughout the season.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>When to use it</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Any growth stage</strong> — a foliar tonic to nourish crops and boost resistance.</li>\n<li><strong>Dilution</strong> — <strong>1 L bio-ferment : 1 L water</strong> (or 10 L : 10 L) in a 20 L spray pump.</li>\n<li><strong>Before use</strong> — shake the container well for a uniform mix; open, measure what you need, and re-seal immediately.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Materials</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fresh milk — <strong>2 L</strong> (or <strong>4 L</strong> whey)</li>\n<li>Fresh cow dung — <strong>10 kg</strong> (un-vaccinated cow, kept out of sun)</li>\n<li>Molasses — <strong>2 L</strong>; wood ash — <strong>1 kg</strong></li>\n<li>Activated MM solution — <strong>2 L</strong>; clean water — <strong>20 L</strong></li>\n<li>30 L drum, metal ring fastener, hose and water bottle for the airlock</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How to make it</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Load the drum.</strong> Put in <strong>2 L milk</strong>, then <strong>10 kg fresh cow dung</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Sweeten and add ash.</strong> Dilute <strong>2 L molasses in 20 L water</strong>, add it plus <strong>1 kg wood ash</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Add the microbes.</strong> Stir in <strong>2 L activated MM</strong> until uniform; pick out wood chips. No acidic juices.</li>\n<li><strong>Seal.</strong> Fasten the lid airtight with the metal ring.</li>\n<li><strong>Airlock.</strong> Run a hose from the lid into a bottle of water so gases bubble out and no oxygen returns.</li>\n<li><strong>Wait 25 days.</strong> Keep under shelter, away from sun and rain. Do not open before <strong>day 25</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Signs it worked / troubleshooting</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>Good:</strong> steady gas bubbles rising through the water-bottle airlock as it ferments.</li>\n<li>⚠️ <strong>No bubbles</strong> = poor seal or weak MM → check the lid and airlock are airtight.</li>\n<li>🚫 <strong>Opened early or contaminated with acidic juice</strong> = spoiled batch → keep it sealed the full 25 days and avoid citrus.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How to store</h2>\n<p>Keep the sealed drum under shelter, protected from sun and rain. Ready at <strong>25 days</strong>; open only when needed and re-close immediately. Apply diluted <strong>1:1</strong> with water.</p>\n",
