    "bodyHtml": "<h2>What it is</h2>\n<p>Seawater carries the full spread of ocean <strong>minerals</strong> — regarded in Natural Farming as essential\nalongside NPK. Left in a bowl for a day, it picks up <strong>airborne microbes</strong>; when land microbes meet\nsea minerals and microbes the result is a fertile, brackish energy source that feeds crops and\nlivestock. Rice-washed water and FPJ deepen the effect.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>On the Nutritive Cycle:</strong> Seawater is both a <em>reproductive</em> input — it sweetens ripening fruit —\nand an <em>all-stages</em> mineral and microbial tonic for soil and stock.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>When to use it</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sweeten fruit</strong> — add <strong>WS-Ca</strong> to diluted seawater, spray <strong>twice in one month</strong>, then again <strong>20 days before harvest</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>General mineral feed</strong> — dilute <strong>1 L seawater : 30 L water</strong> (sun-dried salt is instead 2 ml per 1000 ml).</li>\n<li><strong>Soil application</strong> — apply sun-dried salt at <strong>5 kg per 10 acres</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Livestock</strong> — to prevent summer feather loss in chickens, mix BRV (200) and WS-Ca (500) into diluted seawater and feed once every two days.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Materials</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Surface seawater — <strong>1 L</strong> per <strong>30 L</strong> of dilution water</li>\n<li>A large bowl for aging</li>\n<li>Optional: rice-washed water and FPJ (<strong>5 ml</strong> each), WS-Ca, OHN</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How to make it</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Skim the surface.</strong> The deeper the sea, the higher the salt — so collect surface seawater.</li>\n<li><strong>Age one day.</strong> Pour it into a large bowl and leave it a day to let airborne microbes go in.</li>\n<li><strong>Enrich (optional).</strong> Add rice-washed water and FPJ at <strong>5 ml</strong> each; rice-washed water acts like yeast, and OHN makes it stronger still.</li>\n<li><strong>Dilute to use.</strong> Mix <strong>1 L</strong> of seawater into <strong>30 L</strong> of water before applying.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Signs it worked / troubleshooting</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>Good:</strong> sweeter, more aromatic fruit after seawater-plus-WS-Ca sprays; healthy, well-feathered stock.</li>\n<li>⚠️ <strong>Leaf or salt burn</strong> = too concentrated → hold the <strong>1:30</strong> dilution and don&#39;t over-apply salt.</li>\n<li>🚫 <strong>Foul, rotten smell in stored seawater</strong> = spoiled → discard and collect fresh surface water.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How to store</h2>\n<p>Keep the aged seawater cool and shaded. Use diluted batches promptly rather than storing them long.</p>\n",
    "searchText": "seawater & fermented seawater sw surface seawater, aged a day to catch airborne microbes — a full mineral bath that sweetens fruit and energizes soil and stock. minerals microbes seawater minerals salt reproductive microbes fruit surface seawater water (for dilution) what it is seawater carries the full spread of ocean minerals — regarded in natural farming as essential alongside npk. left in a bowl for a day, it picks up airborne microbes ; when land microbes meet sea minerals and microbes the result is a fertile, brackish energy source that feeds crops and livestock. rice washed water and fpj deepen the effect. on the nutritive cycle: seawater is both a reproductive input — it sweetens ripening fruit — and an all stages mineral and microbial tonic for soil and stock. when to use it sweeten fruit — add ws ca to diluted seawater, spray twice in one month , then again 20 days before harvest . general mineral feed — dilute 1 l seawater : 30 l water (sun dried salt is instead 2 ml per 1000 ml). soil application — apply sun dried salt at 5 kg per 10 acres . livestock — to prevent summer feather loss in chickens, mix brv (200) and ws ca (500) into diluted seawater and feed once every two days. materials surface seawater — 1 l per 30 l of dilution water a large bowl for aging optional: rice washed water and fpj ( 5 ml each), ws ca, ohn how to make it 1. skim the surface. the deeper the sea, the higher the salt — so collect surface seawater. 2. age one day. pour it into a large bowl and leave it a day to let airborne microbes go in. 3. enrich (optional). add rice washed water and fpj at 5 ml each; rice washed water acts like yeast, and ohn makes it stronger still. 4. dilute to use. mix 1 l of seawater into 30 l of water before applying. signs it worked / troubleshooting ✅ good: sweeter, more aromatic fruit after seawater plus ws ca sprays; healthy, well feathered stock. ⚠️ leaf or salt burn = too concentrated → hold the 1:30 dilution and don't over apply salt. 🚫 foul, rotten smell in stored seawater = spoiled → discard and collect fresh surface water. how to store keep the aged seawater cool and shaded. use diluted batches promptly rather than storing them long."
